{
 "_doc": "Puppet cuts. Coordinates are pixels in each ink piece (assets/engravings/ink/<piece>.png). For each figure, SAM (ViT-B, scripts/segment.py) cuts the figure from its vignette with a box and positive/negative points. Each part is then cut from the figure the same way, clipped to the figure. pivot = the hinge, in piece pixels; parent = the layer the part rides on; z = stacking order within the figure (higher in front). scripts/puppet_build.py turns the masks into layers. Every hole a cut leaves is filled by texture synthesis from the engraving around it (scripts/puppet_build.py). A part with 'cut' skips SAM: its mask is the union of the cut's polygons and strips ([x0, y0, x1, y1, width], for spears and blades), not clipped: it extends the figure. 'tight' polygons keep only the engraved strokes inside them. Since C2's pose test (the human: bits of every pose that should move didn't), every moving part is a hand cut traced over the ink on a coordinate grid, except Prudence's head and jaw and Mercury's head, wing and two legs, which SAM cut whole.",
